      "measure.block_reduce": "Ordinary default sums own typed block arithmetic and output partitioning. NumPy padding, block-view metadata, storage/layout preparation and allocation remain providers; custom functions/kwargs, complex padding and exceptional/type-frontier sums use literal primitive reducers without native sum credit. Half sums require original padded native/aligned C storage and block volume<=np.getbufsize(); other half layouts or buffered reductions remain literal providers and open native-coverage work. Timed default image calls include the entire padding, summation and allocation path; the frozen per-block 2*gamma_m*S checker runs outside timing."
